%% 05-working-slot.mmd
%% What replaced the five-state machine: a task is queued, or it holds the working
%% slot, or it is neither. There is no third place for it to be, and so no state
%% column that can disagree with where the task actually is.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Queued<br/>(a message_queue row)" as Queued
    state "Paused<br/>(in_process = 1)" as Paused
    state "Working<br/>(the in-memory slot)" as Working
    state "Summary phase<br/>(same slot, priority raised<br/>to [TRUTHFUL-REPORT])" as Summary

    [*] --> Queued : send() admits it

    Queued --> Working : advance() -- slot empty,<br/>or this head STRICTLY beats<br/>the working task

    Working --> Paused : displaced by a higher-priority<br/>arrival. stop_remote_execution first,<br/>THEN the swap -- a stop that fails<br/>UNEXPECTEDLY leaves everything as it was.<br/>A remote that refuses BY DESIGN is recorded<br/>on uncancelled_displacements and the swap<br/>proceeds anyway.<br/><br/>Also reached by a FAILED DELIVERY:<br/>_requeue puts the task back, paused.

    Paused --> Working : advance() picks it before other tasks<br/>OF ITS OWN LABEL, and never before a<br/>different one -- [QUERY] and [ERROR] share<br/>a priority, so a global tie-break would have<br/>a paused [QUERY] beat a fresh [ERROR] and the<br/>Caller\'s correction would never arrive.<br/><br/>EXCEPT a paused WAIT: awaiting_resolution is<br/>read AHEAD of priority, so it outranks every<br/>other row in this agent\'s queue, across labels.<br/><br/>The prompt depends on what resumed --<br/>a plain pause gets one line, "Resume your<br/>previous [RESEARCH]." A summary phase gets<br/>the full report request again. A wait gets<br/>NOTHING rendered and NOTHING delivered.

    Working --> Summary : the work finished and the label<br/>was [RESEARCH] -- it owes a summary,<br/>and the summary is a SECOND exchange<br/>in the SAME slot, not a queued message

    Summary --> [*] : summary pushed to the Caller<br/>as [TRUTHFUL-REPORT]

    Working --> [*] : label_caps.reply_behavior:<br/>[QUERY] -> [MESSAGE-RESPONSE],<br/>[ERROR] -> [MESSAGE-RESPONSE],<br/>[TRUTHFUL-REPORT] and [MESSAGE-RESPONSE] -> NOTHING.<br/>([RESEARCH] -> [TRUTHFUL-REPORT], but by way of<br/>the summary phase above, never from here.)

    note right of Working
        A slot can also hold a WAIT: the agent's
        own unanswered [QUERY] or [ERROR], put
        there by its own send(). No queue row
        backs it, nothing is rendered for it, and
        it is discarded the moment the answer
        arrives. It holds at its natural priority
        of 2, so only a [TRUTHFUL-REPORT] can take
        the slot from it -- and a wait displaced
        that way goes back to the queue carrying
        awaiting_resolution = 1, which makes it
        outrank everything else in that agent's
        queue and re-enter the wait rather than
        come back as work it already asked.

        An agent already waiting is refused a
        second question, already_awaiting_an_answer.

        The wait ends only on a [MESSAGE-RESPONSE],
        which advance looks up BY LABEL rather than
        from the head -- the answer sits at priority
        3, so a head read would find higher-priority
        paused work and deadlock forever. Its row is
        consumed without being promoted, and folded
        into what comes next in one of three shapes:
        the next job quoted in full, the agent's own
        paused work named by label, or the response
        alone when the queue is empty.
    end note

    note left of Summary
        The reply for two of the five labels is
        NOTHING. Without a terminating label,
        every completed task would produce a
        message that produced a task, and two
        agents would talk until one was archived.
    end note
